  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Creation inside an atom and across a cut",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Native creation keeps atoms whole and reads the direction of the cuts between them. The Fano plane's creation map is complete: every removal creates at every other line, so its seven lines form one block (21 of 21 pairs mutual). For a Fano atom attached at a line, creation among its own lines equals the Fano plane's (proved: the rest of the space is a knot space minus that line, so it forces the ports constant and the screening lemma applies), so its lines form a block; checked on 6 designs, 42 of 42 entries each. For a Fano atom attached at a point the same holds on all 10 designs tested (30 of 30 entries each), unproved. Across a cut between two atoms (17 cuts in 21 spaces: designs and every three-fold space up to 19 points), an emitter line and a cut line of the receiver create at each other (294 of 294 pairs), while the receiver's intact lines create at the emitter's lines and the emitter's removals never create at them (382 of 382): creation runs one way, against the cut's direction. Lines sharing two points never create at each other: census 58's three such pairs alone, and 40 of 40 pairs in the spaces tested.",
